  },
  {
   "v": "lavrov",
   "t": "Она немного поплачет и вернётся.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'She will cry a little and return.' Future tense verbs describing what Lavrov expects her to do.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "lyova",
   "t": "Вы уверены в этом?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Are you sure about that?' Sokolov doubts that a mother would tolerate such humiliation.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "lavrov",
   "t": "У неё просто нет выбора.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'She simply has no choice.' Notice the 'of' form after the negative word for 'there is no'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "lavrov",
   "t": "Куда она теперь денется?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Where can she go now?' A common Russian rhetorical idiom meaning 'she has nowhere else to turn'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
